In my album cover design, I focused on creating a calm yet emotionally rich fall atmosphere using red and pink tones to symbolize warmth, nostalgia, and quiet reflection. The composition centers on a small wooden boat resting near the edge of a lake, surrounded by trees glowing in soft autumn light. I wanted the viewer to feel a sense of stillness and memory, as if the scene captures a fleeting moment before the season changes. The mist hovering above the water adds depth and mystery, while the reflection of the trees in the lake creates balance and harmony. I chose a vintage texture and subtle grain to give the image a timeless quality, echoing the feeling of an old record cover. Overall, this piece expresses how color and light can evoke emotion — turning a simple landscape into a visual metaphor for peace and introspection.
